1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,078
Every retailer faces the same balancing act.

2
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:06,411
Order too little, and customers find empty
shelves.

3
00:00:06,461 --> 00:00:11,442
Order too much, and cash gets trapped in stock
that may never sell.

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,456
The problem?

5
00:00:15,506 --> 00:00:19,453
The information needed to make better
decisions is scattered.

6
00:00:19,503 --> 00:00:24,182
Sales sit in the POS, while supplier updates
arrive through spreadsheets,

7
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:25,959
PDFs, and emails.

8
00:00:26,009 --> 00:00:28,600
Critical changes can easily go unnoticed.

9
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:34,537
A delayed delivery or an overlooked price
increase can change what a retailer should

10
00:00:34,587 --> 00:00:36,977
order. Without connecting these signals,

11
00:00:37,027 --> 00:00:39,515
purchasing becomes a costly guessing game.

12
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:43,036
StockPulse turns scattered supplier updates,

13
00:00:43,086 --> 00:00:47,070
demand forecasts, and stock risks into
precise,

14
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:48,746
budget-aware purchasing decisions.

15
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,689
Let's follow one purchasing scenario.

16
00:00:52,739 --> 00:00:57,316
A supplier changes Cola's delivery time from
five days to eight,

17
00:00:57,366 --> 00:00:59,350
while increasing its price.

18
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:02,358
StockPulse extracts these changes into
structured data,

19
00:01:02,408 --> 00:01:06,246
ready for human review before they affect
purchasing decisions.

20
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:12,618
Next, dedicated time-series models forecast
future demand.

21
00:01:12,668 --> 00:01:15,577
StockPulse compares their predictions with a
baseline,

22
00:01:15,627 --> 00:01:20,366
helping retailers understand what they may
need in the coming weeks.

23
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:24,599
The goal is to act before a shortage becomes
urgent.

24
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:31,304
But demand is only half the picture.

25
00:01:31,354 --> 00:01:37,186
With delivery taking longer, current stock may
run out before the next shipment arrives.

26
00:01:37,236 --> 00:01:41,371
StockPulse combines inventory and lead-time
information to flag products that need

27
00:01:41,421 --> 00:01:42,021
attention.

28
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:48,452
Now comes the key decision:

29
00:01:48,502 --> 00:01:50,894
what should the retailer order?

30
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:53,501
StockPulse calculates replenishment using
expected demand,

31
00:01:53,551 --> 00:01:57,104
lead time, safety stock, and incoming orders.

32
00:01:57,154 --> 00:02:02,723
When the budget is limited, it prioritizes
critical products and explains the trade-offs,

33
00:02:02,773 --> 00:02:06,210
so every recommendation has a reason behind
it.

34
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:14,458
The procurement agent turns those calculations
into a clear explanation and a purchase order

35
00:02:14,508 --> 00:02:15,212
draft.

36
00:02:15,262 --> 00:02:19,847
The logic remains auditable, and the agent
cannot approve the order.

37
00:02:19,897 --> 00:02:22,357
The retailer makes the final decision.

38
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,621
From supplier documents to forecasts,

39
00:02:28,671 --> 00:02:30,744
risk detection, and replenishment,

40
00:02:30,794 --> 00:02:33,811
StockPulse brings the purchasing workflow
together.

41
00:02:33,861 --> 00:02:36,619
It is designed for independent retailers,

42
00:02:36,669 --> 00:02:41,822
specialty grocers, and small wholesalers
working with POS data and spreadsheets.

43
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:50,439
Our approach combines AI with dependable
business logic.

44
00:02:50,489 --> 00:02:53,888
Language models interpret documents and
explain recommendations,

45
00:02:53,938 --> 00:02:58,077
while deterministic code calculates risk and
order quantities.

46
00:02:58,127 --> 00:03:00,334
AMD infrastructure, Instinct GPUs,

47
00:03:00,384 --> 00:03:03,319
and ROCm support our AI workload,

48
00:03:03,369 --> 00:03:07,681
with privacy and access controls built into
the deployment.

49
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,015
Fewer empty shelves.

50
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:14,534
Less cash tied up in excess stock.

51
00:03:14,584 --> 00:03:18,243
Smarter purchasing, with decisions retailers
can understand.

52
00:03:18,293 --> 00:03:19,769
This is StockPulse.

